# Hide desktop/KDE crash notifications for expected GPU-process crashes.
#
# On some driver/hardware combinations the GPU process SIGSEGVs while probing
# Vulkan (or GL). Chromium then restarts it without that backend and the
# browser keeps working. That happens before the GPU sandbox makes the
# process non-dumpable, so systemd-coredump + DrKonqi show a KDE
# notification. Disable kernel core dumps for the GPU process only.
# Also skip GPU-process Crashpad dumps in Helium's optional crash dialog.
# Vulkan stays enabled so machines where it works still get it.

